# Walkthrough: Full-Screen Focus Mode

I have successfully transitioned the Focus page from a constrained windowed layout to a full-screen immersive experience.

## Changes Made

### Focus Page Layout
- **Removed the centered card container**: The "windowed" border and inner shadow have been removed, allowing the content to breathe.
- **Expanded to Full Viewport**: The content area now fills the width and height of the screen below the header.
- **Immersive Glassmorphism**: For the task list on the right, I've implemented a deeper glassmorphic look (`bg-black/20`, `backdrop-blur-xl`) that integrates beautifully with the atmospheric backgrounds.
- **Centered Focus Area**: The timer and mode selectors are now perfectly centered in the middle column, creating a strong focal point.
- **Improved Spacing**: Increased padding and gap sizes for a more premium, high-end feel.

### Component Logic
- **Spotify Integration**: Maintain high-quality Spotify player integration on the left side (when enabled), now with more breathing room.
- **Task List**: Moved to a dedicated sidebar-style container on the right that persists in a visible state on larger screens.

## Verification Results

### Visual Audit
- [x] The page occupies 100% of the width and height (below the header).
- [x] Atmospheric backgrounds (Animated, Image, Gradient) cover the entire screen.
- [x] The dark overlay ensures all white text and icons are perfectly legible.
- [x] The "Focusing On" task list on the right feels premium and integrated.

### Functional Check
- [x] Timer start/pause/reset works correctly.
- [x] Mode switching (Focus, Short Break, Long Break) is functional.
- [x] Spotify player controls and visibility toggle correctly.
- [x] Task selection and completion logic remains intact.

> [!TIP]
> Try switching between different **Animated Presets** (like Matrix or Starfield) in the Customise menu to see how they now fill your entire workspace!
